---
// Draft Privacy Policy (OS-294). Kept truthful to the current stack — no
// claims about capabilities (e.g. self-serve export/erasure) we don't have
// yet. The analytics/cookies section is a placeholder until OS-281 (M5)
// picks a tool; revisit alongside OS-297.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 13, 2026';

const sections = [
	{ id: 'scope', label: 'Scope' },
	{ id: 'what-we-collect', label: 'What we collect' },
	{ id: 'how-we-use-it', label: 'How we use it' },
	{ id: 'who-we-share-it-with', label: 'Who we share it with' },
	{ id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies & similar technologies' },
	{ id: 'retention', label: 'Data retention' },
	{ id: 'your-rights', label: 'Your rights' },
	{ id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
	{ id: 'international-transfer', label: 'International transfer' },
	{ id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to this policy' },
	{ id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy — OrderSail"
	description="What OrderSail collects, why, who it's shared with, and how to exercise your privacy rights."
>
	<section class="head">
		<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
		<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="lede">Last updated {lastUpdated}.</p>
	</section>

	<nav class="toc" aria-label="Sections on this page">
		<ol>
			{
				sections.map((s) => (
					<li>
						<a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.label}</a>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ol>
	</nav>

	<article class="legal">
		<h2 id="scope">Scope</h2>
		<p>
			This policy covers the OrderSail marketing site (ordersail.com), the
			merchant dashboard, the storefront and point-of-sale apps, and the API —
			together, the "Service." It describes what we collect from merchants who
			run a shop on OrderSail and from their customers ("buyers") who place
			orders through it.
		</p>

		<h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Merchant account data:</strong> name, email, business details, and
			staff you invite to your account.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Buyer & order data, via merchants:</strong> when someone places an
			order on a merchant's storefront, we process the buyer's name, email,
			and shipping address, and the order/cart contents, on that merchant's
			behalf.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Payment data:</strong> card details go directly to Stripe — we
			never see or store them. We keep records of the transaction (amount,
			status, payout) but no cardholder data.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Usage data:</strong> standard web server logs (IP address,
			timestamps, requests) across the Service.
		</p>

		<h2 id="how-we-use-it">How we use it</h2>
		<p>
			To operate the Service: creating accounts, processing orders and
			payments, arranging shipping, sending transactional email (order
			confirmations, receipts, account notices), and providing support.
		</p>

		<h2 id="who-we-share-it-with">Who we share it with</h2>
		<p>We share data with the processors that make the Service work:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payment processing and payouts.</li>
			<li><strong>Shippo</strong> — shipping labels and carrier rates, which requires full pickup/delivery addresses.</li>
			<li><strong>Amazon Web Services (SES)</strong> — sending transactional email.</li>
			<li><strong>Amazon Web Services</strong> — hosting for the Service and its data.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			We don't sell personal data, and we don't share it with anyone else
			except to comply with the law or protect the Service from fraud and
			abuse.
		</p>

		<h2 id="cookies">Cookies & similar technologies</h2>
		<p>
			The marketing site (ordersail.com) does not currently set any cookies,
			including for analytics — we haven't added a web analytics tool yet.
			When we do, this section and our cookie disclosure will be updated
			before it ships.
		</p>
		<p>
			The merchant dashboard uses one strictly-necessary, HTTP-only session
			cookie to keep you signed in. It isn't used for tracking or
			advertising. Other parts of the Service (the storefront and API) use
			bearer tokens instead of cookies.
		</p>

		<h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>
		<p>
			We keep account and order data for as long as an account is active, and
			for a reasonable period afterward for legal, accounting, and fraud-prevention
			purposes. We're a small team without automated data-aging yet — if
			you'd like something deleted sooner, contact us (below) and we'll
			handle it manually.
		</p>

		<h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
		<p>
			Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct,
			export, or delete your personal data, or to object to certain
			processing. We don't yet have a self-service tool for this — email <a
				href="/contact">privacy@ordersail.com</a
			> and we'll fulfill the request directly. Merchants can already pull
			their catalog, orders, and customer data through the API at any time.
		</p>

		<h2 id="children">Children</h2>
		<p>
			The Service isn't directed at children, and you must be at least 18 (or
			the age of majority where you live) to hold an OrderSail account. We
			don't knowingly collect data from children.
		</p>

		<h2 id="international-transfer">International transfer</h2>
		<p>
			OrderSail and its processors are based in the United States. If you're
			accessing the Service from outside the U.S., your data will be
			transferred to and processed in the U.S. Merchants who need a formal
			transfer mechanism for their own compliance can request our Data
			Processing Agreement (contact below).
		</p>

		<h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
		<p>
			We may update this policy as the Service changes. We'll update the "last
			updated" date above, and for material changes we'll make a reasonable
			effort to notify account owners directly.
		</p>

		<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Privacy questions or requests: <a href="mailto:privacy@ordersail.com"
				>privacy@ordersail.com</a
			>, or use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> for any other channel.
		</p>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.head {
		padding: 40px 0 32px;
	}
	.head h1 {
		font-family: Georgia, serif;
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
		line-height: 1.1;
		font-weight: 400;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		margin: 0 0 14px;
	}
	.lede {
		font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
		font-size: 0.86rem;
		color: var(--ink-dim);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.toc {
		padding: 24px 0 32px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
		margin-bottom: 40px;
	}
	.toc ol {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 10px 28px;
	}
	.toc a {
		font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		text-decoration: none;
		color: var(--ink-dim);
	}
	.toc a:hover {
		color: var(--ink);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	.legal {
		max-width: 68ch;
		padding-bottom: 90px;
		font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
		font-size: 0.98rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--ink);
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-family: Georgia, serif;
		font-size: 1.3rem;
		font-weight: 400;
		margin: 40px 0 12px;
		scroll-margin-top: 24px;
	}
	.legal p {
		margin: 0 0 16px;
	}
	.legal ul {
		margin: 0 0 16px;
		padding-left: 1.2em;
	}
	.legal li {
		margin: 0 0 8px;
	}
	.legal a {
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}
</style>
